SUMMARY:An affirmative solution to the generalized Busemann-Petty problem with subspaces dimensions 2 and 3
DESCRIPTION:The generalized Busemann--Petty problem asks whether two origin-symmetric convex bodies in $\\mathbb{R}^n$ having larger volume of all $m$-dimensional sections necessarily have larger volume. When $m\\geq 4$\, this is known to be false\, but the cases $m=2\, 3$ for $n\\geq 5$ have remained open since the 1990s. In this work\, we resolve these cases. Together with the known results\, the generalized Busema\nhttps://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17073/
LOCATION:IHP - Bâtiment Borel
URL:https://indico.math.cnrs.fr/event/17073/
